  "worked_solution": "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{2}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u20613-2\\operatorname{ln}\u20611 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u20613.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $2\\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$",
